# Charge a Necromancer by character generation, then create undead with the
# wizard's Create Corporeal Undead and photograph the Group CR Totals block.
# bd inc-1n74, tools/check_necro_undead_pool.sh.
#
# THE GRANT UNDER TEST COMES FROM lib/classes.irh AT GENERATION TIME. A level-1
# Necromancer is given BONUS_PHD of magnitude 1 against PHD_UNDEAD; a mage of
# any other school is not. So this script must RUN the chargen -- loading a
# frozen .sav would bake in whichever lib made that save, and the check could
# not go red on the lib mutation (see tools/check_necro_undead_pool.sh).
#
# The chargen below is tools/keys/chargen-mage.keys' character (male orc mage,
# neutral, Point Buy attributes, first two feats, three RIGHTs per skill) with
# one change: the school is Necromancy. The comparison script
# tools/keys/necro-undead-pool-mage.keys is the same file with Evocation, so the
# only difference between the two characters is the school.
#
# WHY THERE ARE SEVERAL CASTS. One wight proves the GRANT (PHD UNDEAD 2 / 1).
# The admission change in Monster::MakeCompanion's PHD_UNDEAD branch needs more:
# it must REFUSE a created undead once undead + magic + party are full. So after
# the grant reading this script raises wight after wight on the corpses the
# level leaves behind. Each cast is photographed twice: the cast screen, which
# carries the caller's own verdict ("The dead rise!" or "shifts briefly, but
# does not move", lib/abilities.irh:179/187), and the wizard Group CR Totals
# block, which carries the count that actually joined. The message window is
# only a few lines deep and a created undead angers many gods, so the window
# can scroll "The dead rise!" away; the pool reading is the reliable count.
# On the fixed code the third attempt is refused and the pool stops growing.
# The mutated run (tools/check_necro_undead_pool.sh --prove-red) sends the
# PHD_UNDEAD case back to the generic branch, which never refuses here.
#
# TARGETING. Every cast aims at a corpse this script made itself. Five ghouls
# are summoned on the squares 1 to 5 east of the player, and Genocide
# Everything kills them where they stand, so each leaves a corpse on a known
# square whatever the seed. A ghoul has no Gear: line, so nothing it drops
# lies on top of its corpse; the target prompt reads only the first thing on a
# square (Term.cpp, m->FirstAt), and a pile whose top is a dagger or a torch
# is an Invalid Target. A black orc or a human carries gear and fails here.
# Ghoul corpses are valid for the spell: the ghoul is a medium humanoid.
# Create Corporeal Undead's target prompt takes 'l' to move the location
# cursor, then RIGHT*n to the nth ghoul corpse. The ring arrows
# cannot be used here -- after the first wight they include the wights
# themselves, and the prompt stops on one.
#
# ATTRIBUTES. Point Buy, not a rolled set, so no seed changes them. The party
# pool is TotalLevel + Mod(CHA) (src/Social.cpp, Player::MaxGroupCR), and a
# rolled Charisma moved the count at which cast 2 is refused.
#
# THE KNOWLEDGE MESSAGE IS PINNED ON. A refused cast prints "The <corpse> shifts
# briefly, but does not move." The corpse name carries "(fresh, DC 25)", which
# makes the sentence 66 columns wide against a 64-column message window, so it
# wraps and no screen holds the whole phrase -- unless the line already holds
# an earlier message, which moves the wrap. A Knowledge message ("Using your
# knowledge of the undead, you realize ...") is that earlier message, and it
# fires only when a skill check passes. tools/check_necro_undead_pool.sh sets
# INCURSION_RUNTO_SKILL_ROLL=20, so the check always passes and the sentence
# always lands whole on the cast screen. Pinned to 1 the message never fires and
# no screen carries the phrase.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes
@choose "Orc"
@choose "Orc (Standard)"
@choose "Mage"
p       # Abort to Point Buy; every attribute starts at 8, with 75 points
        # STR 14, DEX 16, CON 18, INT 18, WIS 12, CHA 16, LUC 17 == exactly 75
        # (the orc takes -2 Charisma: the character reads CHA 14, as the seed-1 one did)
RIGHT*6 DOWN RIGHT*8 DOWN RIGHT*10 DOWN RIGHT*10 DOWN RIGHT*4 DOWN RIGHT*8 DOWN RIGHT*9
ENTER
y       # Are these your final stats? -- yes
@choose "Neutral"
@choose "Necromancy"
a       # First feat
a       # Second feat
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y
y       # Worship the offered god
a       # Personality archetype
@expect "Learn Spells: Level"    # the starting-spells checklist
SPACE DOWN SPACE DOWN SPACE DOWN SPACE DOWN    # mark the first rows; a full level refuses the rest
SPACE DOWN SPACE DOWN SPACE DOWN SPACE DOWN
ENTER
x       # Dismiss the arrival room description

@until "Things in View" ESC
w y                     # Enter wizard mode and confirm.

# Infinite Mana (Table row 8) lets a level 1 mage cast a level 5 spell.
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*7 SPACE
ESC

# Create Corporeal Undead is not on the mage list; Learn Any Spell makes it known.
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Create Corporeal Undead" ENTER

# Five ghouls on known squares east of the player, one corpse apiece after the
# genocide below. Summon lands on the Q_LOC cursor square (src/Debug.cpp:679).
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Corporeal Undead"
@choose "ghoul"
RIGHT*1 ENTER
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Corporeal Undead"
@choose "ghoul"
RIGHT*2 ENTER
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Corporeal Undead"
@choose "ghoul"
RIGHT*3 ENTER
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Corporeal Undead"
@choose "ghoul"
RIGHT*4 ENTER
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Corporeal Undead"
@choose "ghoul"
RIGHT*5 ENTER

# Clear the level. Every monster dies where it stands and leaves a corpse: the
# five orcs' corpses are on the known squares, the level's own are scattered
# wherever the seed put them and are never aimed at.
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Genocide Everything"
SPACE*40                 # dismiss the genocide message chain

# The control reading: no undead yet. Necromancer PHD UNDEAD max 1, other mage 0.
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*200
@dump:group-before
ESC
SPACE*4

# Cast 1: the first ghoul's corpse. This is a real Monster::MakeCompanion(PHD_UNDEAD)
# caller (lib/abilities.irh:177).
m
a
l
RIGHT*1 ENTER
@choose "Wight"
@dump:raised
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*200
@dump:group-after
ESC
SPACE*4

# Cast 2: the second ghoul's corpse. Kept under the fixed code.
m
a
l
RIGHT*2 ENTER
@choose "Wight"
@dump:cast2
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*200
@dump:group2
ESC
SPACE*4

# Cast 3: the third ghoul's corpse. REFUSED under the fixed code.
m
a
l
RIGHT*3 ENTER
@choose "Wight"
@dump:cast3
SPACE*3
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*200
@dump:group3
ESC
SPACE*4

# Cast 4: the fourth ghoul's corpse. REFUSED under the fixed code.
m
a
l
RIGHT*4 ENTER
@choose "Wight"
@dump:cast4
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*200
@dump:group4
ESC
SPACE*4

# Cast 5: the fifth ghoul's corpse. REFUSED under the fixed code.
m
a
l
RIGHT*5 ENTER
@choose "Wight"
@dump:cast5
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*200
@dump:group5
ESC
SPACE*4

@quit
